# ===== ORIGINAL NOTEBOOK CELL 77 =====
# ============================================================
# SECTION F — VALUATION ENGINE
# CELL F6 — REVERSE DCF / MARKET-IMPLIED EXPECTATIONS GAP
#           V1.0.0
# ============================================================
#
# Purpose:
#
#   Translate the difference between:
#
#       current market price
#
#   and:
#
#       F5 final BASE intrinsic value
#
# into economically interpretable market-implied assumptions.
#
#
# OPERATING COMPANIES
# -------------------
#
# Primary reverse-DCF variable:
#
#       additive revenue-growth shift
#
#       g_market,t
#       =
#       g_base,t + Delta_g
#
# for forecast Years 1-5.
#
#
# All other assumptions remain fixed:
#
#       EBIT margin
#       tax rate
#       D&A
#       CapEx
#       working capital
#       discount rate
#       terminal growth
#       exit multiple
#
#
# Solve:
#
#       ReverseDCF_Price(Delta_g)
#       =
#       Current Market Price
#
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# FINANCIAL COMPANIES
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Primary reverse-valuation variable:
#
#       additive ROE shift
#
#       ROE_market,t
#       =
#       ROE_base,t + Delta_ROE
#
#
# Explicit F3 earnings-growth assumptions remain fixed.
#
# Book value is reconciled exactly as in F5A.
#
#
# Solve:
#
#       ReverseRI_Price(Delta_ROE)
#       =
#       Current Market Price
#
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# SECONDARY EXPECTATIONS DIAGNOSTIC
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# F6 also solves analytically for the EXIT MULTIPLE required
# for today's price while keeping ALL explicit base-case
# assumptions unchanged.
#
#
# Therefore each company receives:
#
#   Operating:
#
#       market-implied revenue-growth shift
#       market-implied average revenue growth
#       market-implied exit EV/EBITDA
#
#
#   Financial:
#
#       market-implied ROE shift
#       market-implied average ROE
#       market-implied P/B or P/E
#
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# F6 is DIAGNOSTIC.
#
# It does NOT:
#
#   - change intrinsic value
#   - change F5 confidence
#   - change margin-of-safety thresholds
#   - change ranking
#   - change sector scores
#
#
# It answers:
#
#   "What assumptions does the current market price appear
#    to require, relative to our base case?"
#
#
# Historical backtest remains blocked.
# ============================================================


# ============================================================
# 1. IMPORTS
